From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:08:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] tests: GLM EXL3 at mixed widths, synthetic and a
 checkpoint's own layers

glm-exl3 runs Mia-AiLab's 4-bit experts, 3-bit gate and up over 4-bit
down, and 2/3/4-bit gate/up/down, each projection on its own width
table, decode and prompt chunks (1030 rows, two calls) against float64,
rows as alone, NaN kept to its row.

glm-exl3-layer <ckpt> <layer> <rank> <world> loads one checkpoint layer
through cuda_exl3.load at a rank's TP share and runs it (decode windows
and a prompt chunk) against float64 matrices decoded from the whole
trellises (core's unpack, cut, rotated, scaled), with a planted control
(gate and up swapped) that must fail the same tolerance.

---
 zig/tests/cuda/glm_exl3_layer_tests.zig | 328 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 zig/tests/cuda/glm_exl3_tests.zig       |  49 ++--
 zig/tests/cuda/main.zig                 |   3 +
 3 files changed, 363 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)
